Reading the dump: <material.rawValue>/<blending>/<state>/<w>x<h>
  rawValue 7  = .sidebar             -> sidebar, 220 wide x 722 tall
  rawValue 10 = .headerView          -> tab bar 959x32 and status bar 959x24
  'behind'    = blends with what is behind the WINDOW (the desktop)
  'follows'   = dims when the window loses focus (system behaviour)

If the window were opaque these three views would render as flat grey;
they are the mechanical proof that the chrome is real vibrancy.
